NNAAMMEE
     llooggiinnss — display account information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     llooggiinnss [--aaddmmooppssttuuxx] [--gg _g_r_o_u_p_s] [--ll _l_o_g_i_n_s]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The llooggiinnss utility displays information about user and system accounts.

     The following options are available:

     --aa         Display information about the password change and account ex‐
                piration times for each account.

     --dd         Select accounts with duplicate UIDs.

     --gg _g_r_o_u_p_s  Select accounts that are members of the specified groups.  If
                multiple group names are specified, they must be separated
                with commas.

     --ll _l_o_g_i_n_s  Select accounts matching the specified login names.  If multi‐
                ple names are specified, they must be separated with commas.

     --mm         Show information about secondary groups.

     --oo         Display the information for each account on a single line of
                colon-separated fields.

     --pp         Select accounts with no password.

     --ss         Select system accounts.  These are currently defined as ac‐
                counts with UIDs below 1000, plus the “nobody” account (UID
                65534).

     --tt         Sort selected accounts by name rather than by UID.

     --uu         Select user accounts.  These are currently defined as accounts
                with UIDs above 1000, except the “nobody” account (UID 65534).

     --xx         Display information about each account's home directory and
                shell.

     If multiple selection options are specified, all accounts matching any of
     the selection criteria will be displayed.

     If no selection options are specified, all accounts will be displayed.

